CORE
test-operand.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[shell-unsupported\.[0-9]+\] .*: FAILURE$
--
An operand of test with pathname expansion: one pathname, or the word
itself, is tested; several pathnames make test fail or report an error.
